<title>KENYA: KENYA MAY RAISE RATES ON T-BILLS  - MINISTER.</title>
<headline>KENYA MAY RAISE RATES ON T-BILLS  - MINISTER.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kenya's Finance Minister Musalia Mudavadi said on Thursday the government was prepared to accept higher yields on government securities if forced by circumstances.</p>
<p>&quot;The government, in consultation with the Central Bank of Kenya will, if need be, accept higher interest rates on Treasury Bills in order to ensure it meets its financing requirement while at the same time safeguarding price stability,&quot; he said in a statement.</p>
<p>The full text of the statement will follow shortly.</p>
</text>
